.TH PDFCUBE 1 "October 2026" "pdfcube @VERSION@" "PDFCube Manual"
.SH NAME
pdfcube \- present PDF slides with animated 3D transitions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdfcube
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ presentation.pdf ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdfcube
is a focused PDF presentation viewer with animated cube transitions,
programmed slide timing, and keyboard-controlled zoom regions. Pages are
rendered with Poppler and Cairo and displayed through GTK 4 and OpenGL.
.PP
If no PDF file is supplied, a file chooser is displayed.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
PDF Blinds transitions are rendered as cascading rotating slats, horizontally
or vertically according to the document. PDF Box retains the cube effect.
PDF Split uses two perspective doors on fixed outer hinges: horizontal means
top/bottom flaps, vertical means left/right doors. Outward opens the old page;
inward closes the new page. The document selects axis and direction.
PDF Cover folds the incoming page over the old slide; Uncover peels the old
page away. These use one curved sheet, with PDF direction 0 (right), 90 (up),
180 (left), or 270 (down). Missing or unsupported angles default to right.
PDF Fly moves a page like a leaf on a shallow 3D arc. Direction, inward/outward
motion and starting scale come from the document; arbitrary direction angles
are supported. Invalid starting scales default to full size.
PDF Push treats both pages as shallow padded blocks. The incoming page transfers
momentum to the outgoing page; both compress briefly at their shared contact
edge and recover fully. PDF direction selects right, up, left, or down; missing
or unsupported angles default to right.
PDF Dissolve cracks the outgoing page into irregular glass-like shards, then
moves the fragments away to reveal the destination page.
Other unsupported PDF transitions currently change pages instantly.
PDF transition duration controls the animation; page duration controls how
long automatic playback displays a slide. These are separate values.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display the PDFCube version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bgcolor " " r:g:b"
Set the background color. Each component is a number from 0.0 to 1.0.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-top-color " " r:g:b"
Set the cube cap color. Each component is a number from 0.0 to 1.0.
The Push effect uses the same color for its shallow side faces.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no-fullscreen
Start in a window instead of fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Automatically advance slides using PDF page display durations or the program
specified with
.BR \-\-program .
.TP
.BI \-\-program " n:x:n:x:..."
Set slide durations and following transition types. Durations are in seconds;
.B c
selects a cube transition and
.B p
selects a plain transition.
.B blinds
selects rotating slats with a 750 ms animation.
.B split
selects hinged doors with a 750 ms animation, using the document's axis and
direction (horizontal and inward by default).
.B cover
and
.B uncover
select curved page flips with a 750 ms animation and the document's direction.
.B fly
selects the leaf-like Fly effect with a 750 ms animation and the document's
direction, motion and starting scale.
.B push
selects the soft-block Push effect with a 750 ms animation and the document's
direction.
.B dissolve
selects the glass-shatter Dissolve effect with a 750 ms animation.
.B glitter
selects directional fragments and sparks with a 750 ms animation.
.B wipe
selects a raised physical wiper with a 750 ms animation and the PDF direction
(0/right, 90/up, 180/left, 270/down; other angles default to right).
Both pages retain their fitted aspect ratios.
The last pair is repeated for remaining slides.
For example,
.B \-\-program 5:c:3:p
uses five seconds followed by a cube, then three seconds followed by a plain
transition.
.TP
.B \-\-experimental
Enable optional animation details, currently very thin glass shard edges in
Dissolve. The normal launch timing and velocity are unchanged. Disabled by
default; use \-\-experimental=false to explicitly disable it.
.TP
.BI \-\-performance-log " file.csv"
Buffer animation frame timestamps, frame intervals, CPU submission times,
transition identifiers, progress and preparation state, then write them to the
named CSV file on exit. No file I/O occurs during animation. At 60 Hz, smooth
animation frames should produce intervals close to 16667 microseconds.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
.TP
.B Space, Page Down
Advance using the programmed transition.
.TP
.B c, a
Move forward or backward with a cube transition.
.TP
.B Right, Left, Page Up
Move forward or backward without animation.
.TP
.B h, j, k, l, z
Zoom into the upper-left, upper-right, lower-left, lower-right, or
lower-center region, respectively, using the original camera animation.
Press any zoom key again to return to the full page.
.TP
.B g
Reset the zoom.
.TP
.B f
Toggle fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B t
Toggle automatic advancement.
.TP
.B 1 through 9
Jump to page 5*(n-1). These unmodified keys are page shortcuts.
.TP
.B Ctrl-1 through Ctrl-9
Jump to the corresponding PDF or programmed cube section. The Ctrl modifier
keeps section navigation distinct from the page shortcuts above.
.TP
.B Ctrl-l
Reload the OpenGL resources and redraw.
.TP
.B Escape, Ctrl-q
Quit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Options may be placed in
.IR ~/.pdfcuberc
using Boost Program Options syntax. Command-line options take precedence.
For example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
demo=true
bgcolor=0:0:0
program=5:p
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B pdfcube slides.pdf
Present a PDF in fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B pdfcube --demo --program 5:c slides.pdf
Advance every five seconds with cube transitions.
.TP
.B pdfcube --no-fullscreen --bgcolor 0:0:0 slides.pdf
Present in a window with a black background.
